    "recommendations": "Reducing the concentration of brush and shrubs in the area immediately surrounding the structure would improve defensible space and may reduce fuel continuity across the property. Where shrubs and mixed vegetation are adjacent to the structure, increasing the separation between that vegetation and the building could reduce direct fuel exposure to the structure. Managing scattered shrubs throughout the property to create greater spacing between individual plants may interrupt continuous pathways that could otherwise carry fire toward improvements. Keeping the long driveway clear of encroaching vegetation along its edges would support firefighter access and improve the ability of emergency vehicles to safely reach and exit the property. Because a single access route serves the property, maintaining that route in passable condition at all times is a practical priority for both evacuation and suppression operations. Continued attention to vegetation management near structures and along access routes would support long-term wildfire resilience across the property."
